---

## Internal Linking Rules (Enforce on Every Page)
- Every page must link to at least 3 other Core 30 pages.
- **Service pages** → parent Category Hub + 2 related service pages + 1 city page
- **City pages** → both Category Hubs + 3 relevant service pages
- **Category Hubs** → all child service pages + 3 city pages
- **Homepage** → both hubs + top 3 service pages + top 3 city pages

---

## Schema Markup Requirements
- **Homepage + City Pages:** `LocalBusiness` schema with `areaServed`, `hasOfferCatalog`, `priceRange`
- **Service Pages:** `Service` schema with `serviceType`, `provider`, `areaServed`, `offers.priceSpecification`
- **All Pages:** `BreadcrumbList` + `FAQPage` (3–5 Q&A pairs targeting long-tail questions)
- Schema must be valid JSON-LD. Always validate before shipping.

---

## Brand & Design System
### Colors (Tailwind classes preferred)
| Token | Hex | Tailwind |
|---|---|---|
| Primary Green (CTAs, buttons) | `#22C55E` | `green-500` |
| Deep Green (headers, text) | `#15803D` | `green-700` |
| Light Green (section backgrounds) | `#F0FDF4` | `green-50` |
| Body Text | `#374151` | `gray-700` |
| Card Borders / Backgrounds | `#F9FAFB` | `gray-50` |

### Typography
- `DM Sans` Bold 700 → H1/Display (tracking: -0.02em)
- `DM Sans` SemiBold 600 → H2–H4
- `Inter` Regular 400 → body (line-height: 1.6)
- `JetBrains Mono` → pricing displays, technical specs only

### Design Principles
1. White backgrounds, generous padding — startup aesthetic
2. Green is the ONLY brand color
3. Trust signals above the fold: "Licensed Contractors · Verified Reviews · 4-Hour Response"
4. Real photography only — no stock art
5. Always show price ranges — transparency builds trust
6. Subtle micro-animations on hover/form transitions (no heavy JS)

---

## Conversion & Lead Form Rules
- Every page must have an above-fold CTA: "Get Your Free Estimate — 60 Seconds"
- Secondary CTA: phone number (818 area code)
- The Instant Estimate form is a **5-step multi-step flow** (no full page reload between steps):
  1. Job type selector (EV Charger / Panel Upgrade / Both)
  2. Address / zip (autocomplete)
  3. Panel capacity (Yes 200A / No / Not Sure)
  4. Timeline (ASAP / Within 1 Month / Just Researching)
  5. Photo upload (optional) + contact capture (Name, Phone required; Email optional)
- On submit: fire conversion event, show confirmation with estimated price range
- Lead tiers: Platinum ($350–$400), Gold ($150–$250), Silver ($75–$100)
- Phone is the primary required field — not email

---

## Lead Routing (Backend Logic)
On form submit, trigger all four in parallel:
1. Email to contractor assigned to user's zip (SendGrid)
2. SMS to contractor (Twilio): name, phone, job type, zip
3. Slack notification to #leads channel
4. Log to Airtable: Name, Phone, Email, Job Type, Zip, Panel Photo URL, Timestamp, Contractor Assigned, Status

---

## Content Rules
- **Panel service pages must always frame the service as EV-triggered.** "You need a panel upgrade because your EV charger requires it" — not as a standalone electrical service.
- **City pages require hyper-local signals.** Every city page must include: utility provider name, specific rebate amount + program name, permit authority (city vs. LA County), at least one neighborhood-specific housing stock detail, and decade of construction where relevant.
- **Utility map** (critical for differentiation — no competitor does this):
  - Burbank → Burbank Water & Power (BWP) — up to $500 rebate
  - Glendale → Glendale Water & Power (GWP) — $250 rebate
  - Pasadena → Pasadena Water & Power (PWP) — EV Ready Rebate
  - North Hollywood, Studio City, Van Nuys, Encino, Northridge, San Fernando, Highland Park, Sunland, Tujunga → LADWP — up to $500
  - La Cañada Flintridge, Altadena → Southern California Edison (SCE) — different rebate program; permits through LA County DRP (not a city)
- City page minimum word count: 800–1,200 words
- All city pages must follow the H1/H2 content template from the Master OS (§5.3)
- Do NOT create pages for: Load Calculation Service, Home Electrical Inspection, or any general electrical service

---

## NAP — Must Be Identical Everywhere (Footer, Schema, GBP)
- Business Name: `LA Charge Install`
- Phone: `(818) XXX-XXXX` (update when confirmed — must be 818 area code)
- Schema type: `LocalBusiness` > `Electrician`

---

## What We Are NOT Building
- No contractor-facing dashboard in Phase 1 (Phase 3 feature)
- No live chat widget above the fold (kills PageSpeed)
- No Google Analytics (use Plausible + Vercel Analytics)
- No pages for general electrical work outside EV/panel scope
- No dynamic rendering where SSG works — always prefer static
